{"tool_name":"ms2preproc","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"ms2preproc","home":"http://kirchnerlab.github.com/libmgf","summary":"MGF and dta fragment spectrum preprocessing.","addition_date":"2017-01-17T14:51:28Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:13:47.508136Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"collections":["Proteomics","ms-utils"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:ms2preproc","credit":[{"email":"webmaster@ms-utils.org","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Documentor"],"url":"http://ms-utils.org"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://kirchnerlab.github.io/libmgf/doc/html/index.html"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Read pre-processing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3219"}]}],"name":"ms2preproc","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"msutils_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1002/pmic.200900326","metadata":{"abstract":"The effectiveness of database search algorithms, such as Mascot, Sequest and ProteinPilot is limited by the quality of the input spectra: spurious peaks in MS/MS spectra can jeopardize the correct identification of peptides or reduce their score significantly. Consequently, an efficient preprocessing of MS/MS spectra can increase the sensitivity of peptide identification at reduced file sizes and run time without compromising its specificity. We investigate the performance of 25 MS/MS preprocessing methods on various data sets and make software for improved preprocessing of mgf/dta-files freely available from http://hci.iwr.uni-heidelberg. de/mip/proteomics or http://www. childrenshospital.org/research/steenlab. \u00a9 2009 Wiley-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA.","authors":[{"name":"Hamprecht F.A."},{"name":"Ivanov A.R."},{"name":"Kirchner M."},{"name":"Monigatti F."},{"name":"Rappsilber J."},{"name":"Renard B.Y."},{"name":"Steen H."},{"name":"Steen J.A.J."},{"name":"Winter D."}],"citationCount":63,"date":"2009-11-01T00